":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the smallest such sets it is the lexicographically least by vertex index (the rule of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parallel edges do not matter; isolated vertices are in it."}]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover(bipartition:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover(bipartition:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"König’s minimum vertex cover of a bipartite graph (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to_vertex_cover"},{"type":"text","text":", the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cover): from a maximum matching (Hopcroft–Karp on the sides), Z is the set of vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached from the free left vertices by alternating paths, an edge not in the matching from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left to right, then the matched edge back; the cover is (left ∖ Z) ∪ (right ∩ Z), in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. It is the one minimum cover with the most left vertices, so it does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depend on the matching. O(m √n)."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"bipartition","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bipartition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionV"},{"text":"<","ki